-- Migration 3 -> 4: the settings that follow you between devices.
--
-- Until now every setting was device-local, held in SharedPreferences or
-- java.util.prefs. That was right for some of them and wrong for others, and
-- the difference is who the setting is about:
--
--   about YOU      how far ahead to remind, what time of day, which currency to
--                  show totals in, what a euro is worth -- retyping these on
--                  every device is pure friction
--   about DEVICE   whether *this* phone is allowed to notify, which server it
--                  talks to, which peers it has paired with
--
-- Only the first kind lives here. In particular `reminders_on` stays local, so
-- your phone can nag while your laptop stays quiet -- the case that kept the
-- whole group device-local before this.
--
-- One row per key rather than one row holding all of them. Both would merge,
-- but a single blob means changing the reminder time on your phone and the home
-- currency on your laptop makes the two edits collide, and last-write-wins
-- throws one away. Keyed separately, each lands on its own and both survive.
CREATE TABLE setting (
    id         TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    deleted    INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    value      TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''
);
